---
# yamllint disable rule:line-length
# Half one of the guard for a pipeline that leaves the method unterminated
# (#1122), the cross-method twin of the `count()` guard `101-mark-traversing-count`
# and `142-count-keeps-elidable-stage-native` (#973).
#
# Those two keep a chain native when a bare `count()` the JVM elides ends it in
# the same method body. When the chain is built in one method and returned, the
# terminal lives in the caller and neither of them can see it:
#
#   static Stream<Integer> make() { return W.stream().map(s -> bump(s)); }
#   ... make().count()
#
# The map would be fused into a `mapMulti`, which clears SIZED, and a lambda the
# JVM never ran would run once per element in the caller. Nothing in this body
# can tell what the caller does, so the guard takes the conservative branch:
# a stream that is returned keeps its stages native. This rule records that a
# stream is returned, by stamping an `areturn` that directly follows a call
# answering `Stream`, `IntStream`, `LongStream` or `DoubleStream` with
# `escapes ↦ Φ.true`; `142-returned-stream-keeps-stage-native` then reverts the
# stages in front of it.
#
# It runs here, before any stage is lifted into a Φ.hone.lambda, for the reason
# `101-mark-traversing-count` gives: the call is still a raw opcode carrying its
# own signature. The stamp is an extra operand on the `areturn`, which jeo
# ignores when assembling, and the pattern is closed on the bare `areturn`, so
# the rule cannot re-fire on its own output.
#
# Detection is method-local and errs safe: another, locally consumed pipeline
# in a method that also returns a stream keeps its stages native too, which
# only forfeits a fusion. A stream that leaves the method in another way, say
# stored in a field or passed to a call, is not seen by this rule.
name: mark-escaping-stream
pattern: |
  ⟦
    𝐵-before,
    𝜏-call ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.𝜏-op,
      𝜏-class ↦ 𝑒-class,
      𝜏-method ↦ 𝑒-method,
      𝜏-signature ↦ 𝑒-signature,
      𝐵-call-rest
    ⟧,
    𝜏-return ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.areturn
    ⟧,
    𝐵-after
  ⟧
result: |
  ⟦
    𝐵-before,
    𝜏-call ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.𝜏-op,
      𝜏-class ↦ 𝑒-class,
      𝜏-method ↦ 𝑒-method,
      𝜏-signature ↦ 𝑒-signature,
      𝐵-call-rest
    ⟧,
    𝜏-return ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.areturn,
      escapes ↦ Φ.true
    ⟧,
    𝐵-after
  ⟧
when:
  and:
    - or:
        - eq: [𝜏-op, 'invokeinterface']
        - eq: [𝜏-op, 'invokevirtual']
        - eq: [𝜏-op, 'invokestatic']
    - matches:
        - '^\(.*\)Ljava/util/stream/(Stream|IntStream|LongStream|DoubleStream);$'
        - 𝑒-signature
